+    t.index ["record_type", "record_id", "shard"], name: "index_storage_totals_on_record_type_and_record_id_and_shard", unique: true
+  end
+
   create_table "taggings", id: :uuid, force: :cascade do |t|
     t.uuid "account_id", null: false
     t.uuid "card_id", null: false
diff --git a/docs/storage-usage.md b/docs/storage-usage.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b5b3d2a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/storage-usage.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` return integer byte counts computed in
+background jobs. An empty account or board returns `0`. Reads do not scan
+attachments, load rich text, enqueue jobs, or memoize a stale value on the model.
+
+Counted attachments are:
+
+- Card images (`Card#image`), including draft and closed cards.
+- Files embedded in board public descriptions, card descriptions, and comment bodies.
+
+Avatars, export/import archives, generated variants/previews, remote URLs, and
+unattached uploads do not count. Each attachment association counts once. Reusing
+a blob in another counted location counts it there too; repeated references in a
+single rich-text field use Action Text's single attachment association.
+
+## Background processing
+
+Keep Solid Queue's scheduler and `backend` workers running. The
+`update_storage_usage` recurring task sweeps pending work every minute. Counts are
+eventually consistent: they reflect the last completed rollups, not uploads or
+removals whose jobs have not run yet. Large backlogs may need multiple sweeps.
+
+Attachment mutations mark `Storage::Entry` rows dirty **in the same database
+transaction**. Repeated edits coalesce into one pending entry, so active users do
+not enqueue a recount per edit. Purge/detach paths that bypass Active Record
+destroy callbacks are covered explicitly. Card moves also invalidate their image,
+description, and comment entries in the move transaction.
+
+Each entry stores the last accounted board and byte size. Workers lock entries,
+read current attachment metadata using indexed SQL joins, and atomically commit
+both updated entries and the difference to board/account totals. Removals retain
+an entry until its old usage has been subtracted. Retries and duplicate workers
+cannot count a change twice, and a failed job leaves its work pending for the next
+sweep. Normal rollups cost proportionally to changed attachments, not total
+account/board size.
+
+Totals are divided into 16 fixed shards per account and board. A read sums at most
+16 rows. Workers lock an account **total shard**, not the Account or Board model,
+and serialize matching board-shard updates behind it. Unrelated shards can be
+processed concurrently. Transactions handle at most 100 entries and jobs at most
+100 batches; newer invalidations of already-visited entries wait for the next
+sweep rather than starving later entries. Do not change `SHARD_COUNT` without
+migrating existing entries and totals together.
+
+## Existing data and imports
+
+The daily `reconcile_storage_usage` job backfills pre-existing attachments and
+repairs changes made by bulk operations that bypass callbacks. It is resumable,
+uses bounded batches, and only reads metadata. Imports enqueue an account-scoped
+reconciliation automatically; accounting internals are not exported/imported.
+
+After deploying the migration to an existing installation, start the initial
+backfill immediately rather than waiting for the daily schedule:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'Storage::ReconcileJob.perform_later'
+```
+
+To reconcile a particular account:
+
+```ruby
+account.reconcile_storage_later
+```
+
+The normal minute-by-minute sweep drains the resulting work. Account deletion
+cleans up both pending entries and totals while coordinating with running workers.
